To calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Ph-Flfl Red, we use the given concentration:  
1. The concentration is 0.044% (w/v), which means 0.044 grams of sodium fluoride per 1000 mL of the solution.  
2. Calculate the mass of sodium fluoride in 10 mL:  
   \[
   \text{Mass of sodium fluoride} = \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{1000 \text{ mL}} \times 10 \text{ mL} = 0.0044 \text{ g}
\]  
3. Convert the mass from grams to milligrams:  
   \[
   0.0044 \text{ g} \times 1000 \text{ mg/g} = 4.4 \text{ mg}
\]  
Thus, there are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose.
