</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The entropy change (\(\Delta S\)) for the reaction is calculated as:
\[
\Delta S = \sum \Delta S_{\text{products}} - \sum \Delta S_{\text{reactants}}
\]
Substituting the given molar entropies:
\[
\Delta S = (2 \times 66.5) + (2 \times 248.2) - (2 \times 91.2) - (3 \times 205.1)
\]
\[
\Delta S = (132 + 496.4) - (182.4 + 615.3)
\]
\[
\Delta S = 628.4 - 797.7
\]
\[
\Delta S = -169.3 \, \text{J/mol K}
\]

Thus, the entropy change is \(\boxed{-169.3 \, \text{J/mol K}}\).
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

