<USER_REQUEST>
What is the amount of heat released when 2.5 moles of propane (C3H8) is completely burned in oxygen gas (O2) according to the balanced equation: 

C3H8 + 5O2 → 3CO2 + 4H2O 

given that the standard enthalpy of combustion of propane is -2220 kJ/mol?
</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
To calculate the amount of heat released, we use the following formula:

Heat released = (moles of propane) × (standard enthalpy of combustion of propane)

Given:
Moles of propane = 2.5 moles
Standard enthalpy of combustion of propane = -2220 kJ/mol

Heat released = (2.5 moles) × (-2220 kJ/mol) = -5550 kJ

The negative sign indicates that the reaction is exothermic, meaning heat is released. The magnitude of the negative sign indicates the total amount of heat released.

The answer is $\boxed{5550 \text{ kJ}}$.
</ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>

