","To verify the unitarity condition for the \(S\)-matrix, we start with the definition of the \(S\)--matrix:

\[
S_{mn} = \langle n | S | j \rangle,
\]

where \(|n\rangle\) and \(|j\rangle\) are the eigenstates of the \(S\)-invariant states. The unitarity condition is:

\[
\sum_l S_{lm}^* S_{nl} = \delta_{mn},
\]

where \(S_{lm}^*^*\) is the complex conjugate of \(S_{lm}\), and \(\delta_{mn}\) is the Kronecker delta, which is 1 if \(m = n\) and 0 otherwise.

Substituting the definition of the \(S\-matrix\) into the unitarity condition:

\[
\sum_l \langle n | S | j \rangle^* \langle n | S | j \rangle = \delta_{mn}.
\]

Using the orthogonality of the eigenstates of the \(S\)-invariant states, we can rewrite the sum:

\[
\sum_l \langle n | S^\dagger S | n \rangle = \delta_{mn}.
\]

Since the \(S\)-matrix is unitary, \(S^\dagger S = I\), where \(I\) is the identity matrix. Thus, the inequality simplifies to:

\[
\sum_l \langle n | I | n \rangle = \delta_{mn}.
\]

The identity matrix \(I\) is defined such that \(I_{mn} = \delta_{mn}\), so:

\[
\sum_l \delta_{lm} = \delta_{mn}.
\]

This simplifies to:

\[
\delta_{mn} = \delta_{mn}.
\]

Thus, the unitarity condition is verified. 

