   The heat rejected is \( Q_L = 544 \text{ kJ/kg} \).
   The efficiency is:
   \[
   \eta = \frac{W_C - W_W}{W_C} = frac{W_C - W_w}{Q_L}
   \]
   where \( W_C = W_1 - W_2 \) is the work done during compression and \( W_W = W_3 - W_4 \) is the work done during expansion.
   The efficiency is also:
   \[
   \eta = frac{W_1 - W_2}{W_1} = \dfrac{W_1 - W_2}{W_1}
   \]
   The work done per kg of air is:
   \[
   W = W_1 - W_2 = 1 - \eta = 1 - 0.56 = 0.44 \text{ kJ/kg}
   \]
   The work done per kg of air is \(\boxed{0.44 \text{ kJ/kg}}\).

